 "text": "Under the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006* (RTA), tenancies do not automatically terminate at the end of a fixed term; instead, they automatically convert to month-to-month tenancies. \n\nFurthermore, any clause or agreement requiring a tenant to terminate the tenancy or vacate that is made at the time of entering into the lease—or as a condition of the tenancy agreement—is void. \n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 37(5)",
